<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Latest news from the Middle East, daily international news reports - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24’s coverage and analyses of political and social issues across the Middle East, including Egypt, the Gulf states, Iraq, Israel, Jordan, Lebanon, Saudi Arabia, Syria, Yemen and beyond.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/rss</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:21Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Jordan arrests three following deadly terror attack on church</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bf8921329ae8f17679b36fe9bae6a467b06e98afa4bd9743f4f5c8582c31fdd0</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:21Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T15:12:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261026-jordan-arrests-three-following-deadly-terror-attack-on-church" /><summary type="html">Jordanian authorities on Monday arrested three terrorists following a deadly attack on a church during a funeral procession that killed nine people in the western village of Hammoud. The three assailants – who are Islamic extremists, according the Jordanian director of public security – were injured in a dawn shootout with authorities and are due to be brought before the courts in the nation that supports capital punishment.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Tens of thousands of Israelis living abroad expected to fly in for pivotal vote</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a0e00b463b9434b494dbdda080ae2a452a561df6b0755119fa79e0e40e359dd1</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:21Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T14:20:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tens-of-thousands-of-israelis-living-abroad-expected-to-fly-in-for-pivotal-vote" /><summary type="html">Israelis are preparing to head to the polls on Tuesday (October 27). Unable to vote from abroad, tens of thousands of expatriate citizens have been flying in from across the world to cast their ballots. FRANCE 24's Noga Tarnopolsky met some of them at the airport.</summary></entry><entry><title>Will Netanyahu's security promise win him this election?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0e4db50e9915c5c1d14d2342b10d0288a03330d02b254aa0e72b29b350c48acc</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:21Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T13:52:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261026-will-netanyahu-s-security-promise-win-him-this-election" /><summary type="html">Since the beginning of his political career, Benjamin Netanyahu, Israel's longest-serving prime minister, has campaigned on a promise that he is the only one who will keep the Jewish state safe. As Israelis head to the polls for their first election since the October7 Hamas attacks and the start of the war in Gaza, Netanyahu's strategy might be less effective. FRANCE 24's Gabrielle Nadler explains.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israel braces for national elections seen as a referendum on Netanyahu</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fcb12a8f45892b4d2a02d6a956ef0516843c9c640f540516cb95dc160aa9c439</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:21Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T12:35:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/israel-braces-for-national-elections-seen-as-a-referendum-on-netanyahu" /><summary type="html">Israelis are preparing to head to the polls on Tuesday (October 27)  in the first elections since the October 7th attacks in 2023. Unable to vote abroad, expatriate citizens have been flying in from around the world to participate in a vote widely seen as being a referendum on Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's leadership.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israel: Arab Israeli voters could prove decisive in the upcoming elections</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7db3333c3465dfd0bba35cb8ee6e3679be3ab7c31989b8a6095d41bbd0cb167c</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:21Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T12:13:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/israel-arab-israeli-voters-could-prove-decisive-in-the-upcoming-elections" /><summary type="html">In Israel’s election the vote of Arab Israeli citizens could be crucial for the outcome and fate of Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu who is standing for re-election. Traditionally voting turnout is lower among Arab Israelis than among the rest of the population. But this time some feel it’s their duty more than ever to cast their ballot given the policies and wars undertaken by Netanyahu.</summary></entry><entry><title>A look at the main issues in Israeli elections seen as a referendum on Netanyahu</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3e191088ed8e9eb937ba979d54ab60798bbeab1381bfe3fec10edaa990f17432</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:21Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T11:59:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261026-a-look-at-the-main-issues-in-israeli-elections-seen-as-a-referendum-on-netanyahu" /><summary type="html">Israelis will vote Tuesday (October 27) in the first national elections since Hamas' Oct. 7, 2023, attack in what is widely seen as a referendum on Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's leadership. He rejected ICC war crimes claims and denied corruption as national elections approach. Details by FRANCE 24's correspondent in Jerusalem, Noga Tarnopolsky.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israeli election seen as a referendum: For or against Netanyahu?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a0af5732e28e4f847004712c0e15aa567860996e9523d0ac60326fe55f58ca5f</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:21Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T11:40:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261026-israeli-election-seen-as-a-referendum-for-or-against-netanyahu" /><summary type="html">Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu has led his country almost continuously for nearly 17 years. But will he manage to retain power following Tuesday's election? Netanyahu's latest term has divided Israeli society more than ever and will be marked by the October 7 attacks, his handling of the conflicts in Gaza, Iran and Lebanon, as well as his controversial judicial reform. FRANCE 24's David Gilberg reports, with Lauren Bain.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>Report: IDF chief pushes back on Netanyahu's order</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5d2beb377825be5d62a8171b2abc420b0bb2cbb38282448d2c7ea0ca9d448f89</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:21Z</updated><published>2026-10-25T23:24:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261025-report-idf-pushes-back-on-netanyahu-s-order" /><summary type="html">An extraordinary confrontation at the top of Israel's leadership, just two days before the election. Israeli media report Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu and military chief Eyal Zamir are at odds over Iran. Zamir reportedly fears government instructions could trigger an immediate military escalation and has demanded written authorisation. Netanyahu denies any confrontation. The reports come as he warns Iran could attack Israel to disrupt Tuesday's vote.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israel: Demonstrators rally against government ahead of election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f6521a29606b417b22c5935c3bacfc25e824391d0210c89af005c47b0dce59da</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:21Z</updated><published>2026-10-25T11:38:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/israel-demonstrators-rally-against-government-ahead-of-election--605d00c22edc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/israel-demonstrators-rally-against-government-ahead-of-election" /><summary type="html">In Israel, the anti-Netanyahu movement is mobilising. Thousands gathered in Tel Aviv on Friday to protest against the Israeli government, just three days ahead of a general election widely seen as a referendum on Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu.</summary></entry><entry><title>West Bank: Families forcibly displaced in Hebron</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:57612e45304ac41a7d4a7a4ad7622fa4ad4ce6b57d92608f7cf7a2e04071b273</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:21Z</updated><published>2026-10-25T11:35:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/west-bank-families-forcibly-displaced-in-hebron--c0b8d6b2a6c9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/west-bank-families-forcibly-displaced-in-hebron" /><summary type="html">More Palestinian families have been displaced in the occupied West Bank as Israeli forces continue operations in Hebron, following a deadly shooting that killed two Israeli soldiers on Friday. With elections scheduled for Tuesday, Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu has vowed a heavy response to the attack. Morgaene Ayre has the latest.</summary></entry><entry><title>Thousands take to Tel Aviv's streets for protests against Netanyahu</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f2959af4cb0f67595cde5674f4417c8c9dd4ea8f3f7c6861fabf7112c2714b89</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:21Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T18:21:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261024-thousands-take-to-tel-aviv-streets-for-protests-against-netanyahu--99da939090a4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261024-thousands-take-to-tel-aviv-streets-for-protests-against-netanyahu" /><summary type="html">Thousands marched against Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's government in Tel Aviv on Saturday – just three days before Israel's general election – demanding accountability for the failure to prevent a Hamas-led attack on October 7, 2023, which led to the war in Gaza.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Yemen's Houthi rebels claim new attacks on oil facilities and airports across Saudi Arabia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b038101578ddc4efebaacfb39086c892c4e11e46555d04e0c0dd9e1e9d8f73dc</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:21Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T17:50:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261024-yemen-s-houthi-rebels-claim-new-attacks-on-oil-facilities-and-airports-across-saudi-arabia--98ea10f02978.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261024-yemen-s-houthi-rebels-claim-new-attacks-on-oil-facilities-and-airports-across-saudi-arabia" /><summary type="html">Yemen’s Iran-allied Houthi rebels said they launched attacks at Saudi oil facilities and airports on Saturday while Yemen’s Saudi-backed government ​said the ‌group also fired three ballistic missiles at coast guard sites in ⁠the port city of Aden.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Israel begins demolitions in West Bank</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:598d69477632fc02067a0ddfcc8cc6c658285128a72bfb9f367bc650304ba946</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:21Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T17:13:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/israel-begins-demolitions-in-west-bank--1cdd8864f331.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/israel-begins-demolitions-in-west-bank" /><summary type="html">The Palestinian Authority has called for international pressure on Israel after a Palestinian official said around 1,200 Palestinians in Hebron in the West Bank were forced to leave their homes following an attack on Friday which killed two Israeli soldiers. The head of Hebron's municipality said an additional 1,300 may also be forced to leave.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israel to close all West Bank land crossings on election day</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fe45bc6a82bc8c79cb0dea76cdbc690df903e6c7062a1b920d86361c0397d100</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:21Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T13:52:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261024-israel-to-close-all-land-crossings-with-west-bank-on-election-day--97f1a94dfee6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261024-israel-to-close-all-land-crossings-with-west-bank-on-election-day" /><summary type="html">Israel announced it would be closing all land crossings with the West Bank on the day of next week's parliamentary elections. The measure comes as Israel conducts a large-scale operation in the occupied Palestinian territory and 2,000 residents of Hebron have been displaced from their homes after Palestinian gunmen killed two soldiers in the area.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Israeli forces displace 2,000 Palestinians in Hebron after deadly attack on soldiers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:19542cf89b8c284264680d48ae4ebffcf43cb8ef665207e74e30b35bc07e8341</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:21Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T13:50:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261024-israeli-forces-displace-1-200-palestinians-in-hebron-after-deadly-attack-on-soldiers--bcc1afec2ab7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261024-israeli-forces-displace-1-200-palestinians-in-hebron-after-deadly-attack-on-soldiers" /><summary type="html">The Palestinian Authority called for international pressure on Israel after a Palestinian official said around 1,200 Palestinians in Hebron in the West Bank were forced to leave their homes following an attack on Friday which killed two Israeli soldiers. Israeli defence minister Israel Katz later confirmed in an interview that the displacements had reached the 2,000 mark.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Netanyahu orders West Bank operation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c9a7acade11e01a1f9026dc581712ea37999a98947dcc6476fe6f83db87a968f</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:21Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T10:33:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/netanyahu-orders-west-bank-operation--93ec6832b46e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/netanyahu-orders-west-bank-operation" /><summary type="html">Israel has imposed widespread closures across the occupied West Bank and displaced residents following attacks by Palestinian gunmen that killed two Israeli soldiers. Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu visited the site of the attack near Hebron and instructed security forces to immediately cordon off the city. Morgan Ayre reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Netanyahu weighs West Bank operation ahead of elections: ‘Politically, it will not help anybody’</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f62d8d8da4d8a1f7cacf45f61c188a1329c7b129a8391f7cc387919f1b16e83c</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:21Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T18:26:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261023-netanyahu-weighs-west-bank-operation-ahead-of-elections-politically-it-will-not-help-anybod--82f68804f051.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261023-netanyahu-weighs-west-bank-operation-ahead-of-elections-politically-it-will-not-help-anybody" /><summary type="html">As Israel approaches a consequential parliamentary election amid renewed violence in the occupied West Bank, Yedioth Ahronoth Senior Journalist Ben-Dror Yemini offers a critical assessment of Benjamin Netanyahu's political prospects, the limits of military escalation and the shifting relationship between national security and electoral legitimacy.
 
Since October 7, 2023 "Netanyahu is not popular anymore," Yemini argues, identifying the Hamas-led attacks as a decisive turning point in the Israeli prime minister's public standing.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>How Israeli settlers wearing keffiyehs are attacking West Bank olive groves</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2b4ac8c4a0730694583f7c560d0fcbf24d62c8eab377dd7dc98874f814404c13</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:21Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T17:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261023-how-israeli-settlers-wearing-keffiyehs-are-attacking-west-bank-olive-groves--10563b4076b1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261023-how-israeli-settlers-wearing-keffiyehs-are-attacking-west-bank-olive-groves" /><summary type="html">The olive harvest officially began in the West Bank on October 15, 2026, and it has coincided with an uptick in violence towards Palestinians carried out by both Israeli settlers and soldiers. Meanwhile, the settlers and soldiers have been using social media to promote an aesthetic, Instagram-friendly and nationalistic view of these harvests.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Israel: Could Arab parties play kingmaker in the next Knesset ?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b5af91c7176096622a5ccd3db93ae541f0211d07aec9ba62ca975f21a5661296</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:21Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T17:11:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/israel-could-arab-parties-play-kingmaker-in-the-next-knesset--cd40bcd2e863.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/israel-could-arab-parties-play-kingmaker-in-the-next-knesset" /><summary type="html">As Israelis head to the polls for the first legislative election since Hamas's October 7 attacks, neither Prime Minister Benjamin #Netanyahu's Likud party nor former army chief of staff Gadi #Eisenkot's Yashar party are likely to win a majority of seats in the #Knesset. Turns out, #Israel's Arab parties could have a say in the election's outcome.</summary></entry><entry><title>Gaza : digging up the bodies from under the rubble</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7c54b132edc39cbcf5c04aac34ab80c6914eee3e97c236249e7479d2aa69021b</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:21Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T17:10:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-observers/20261023-gaza-digging-up-the-bodies-from-under-the-rubble--7e525732a26a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-observers/20261023-gaza-digging-up-the-bodies-from-under-the-rubble" /><summary type="html">One year after the ceasefire in Gaza, efforts to recover the bodies buried beneath the rubble are continuing. Civil Defense officials say 1,000 bodies have been recovered so far, but the task remains immense: between 8,000 and 10,000 more are still believed to be buried under the debris, including 3,000 in areas controlled by the Israeli army.</summary><category term="The Observers" /></entry><entry><title>Yes, Israeli settlers are ripping up West Bank olive trees – but this video is fake</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2d43cde94f62536c2e8f60bdc693beb3b8dd1049e8fc20b9ea9cffdd49ad81dc</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:21Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T15:56:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261023-yes-israeli-settlers-ripping-up-west-bank-olive-trees-_-but-this-video-fake--f2a5cae87002.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261023-yes-israeli-settlers-ripping-up-west-bank-olive-trees-%E2%80%93-but-this-video-fake" /><summary type="html">Israeli settlers and soldiers have made a habit of destroying olive trees grown by Palestinian farmers in the West Bank and, in recent days, a video showing some trees being ripped up has circulated online. Just one problem: this particular video was generated by artificial intelligence.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>‘I killed lots of terrorists, but it didn’t make me feel better’: The trauma haunting Israel's elections</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:be2c4136f11daa2d1d2df46a2c83f02d1d4bbeafaa7f0c59091d2669b1323045</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:21Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T14:32:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261023-i-killed-lots-of-terrorists-but-it-didn-t-make-me-feel-better-the-trauma-haunting-israel-s---ad0c03bb89c4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261023-i-killed-lots-of-terrorists-but-it-didn-t-make-me-feel-better-the-trauma-haunting-israel-s-elections" /><summary type="html">After more than three years of war, the number of Israeli soldiers suffering from post-traumatic stress disorder following bloody campaigns in Gaza and Lebanon has risen drastically. In the lead-up to Israel’s crucial legislative elections, FRANCE 24 speaks with soldiers left shell-shocked by the country’s wars.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Several killed, dozens wounded in Jordan church shooting</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:235d0e9d24055a30708c9ef569f6fa587055cbce44312788b982c6ec452d25b0</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:21Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T14:16:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261023-several-killed-dozens-wounded-in-jordan-church-shooting--c1f294640eb8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261023-several-killed-dozens-wounded-in-jordan-church-shooting" /><summary type="html">At least seven people have been killed and 34 others wounded in a church shooting in Jordan, authorities said Friday. The unidentified assailants allegedly attacked the Greek Orthodox church during a funeral in the Karak directorate in the central part of the country.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>War in the Middle East: Israel launches West Bank operations</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:843bd77a7224364ddaac9ef21760b1d995afad58aa858f1cbd7ca76da5b49e0d</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:21Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T12:57:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/war-in-the-middle-east-israel-launches-west-bank-operations--85a7b4908438.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/war-in-the-middle-east-israel-launches-west-bank-operations" /><summary type="html">Palestinian militants wounded five Israelis in an attack on Friday before being killed in a shootout with soldiers, leading Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu to order a lockdown in the occupied West Bank days before Israeli elections. Details by Kethevane Gorjestani, FRANCE 24's International Affairs Editor.</summary></entry><entry><title>Netanyahu orders West Bank closure as attack wounds Israelis before election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:09539450d75ab1b91c3c817f68fdb49f2a0d48d2e81b07a6580008051366b034</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:21Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T10:41:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261023-netanyahu-orders-west-bank-closure-as-attack-wounds-israelis-before-election--fe9233c95ecb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261023-netanyahu-orders-west-bank-closure-as-attack-wounds-israelis-before-election" /><summary type="html">Details by FRANCE 24's correspondent in Jerusalem Noga Tarnopolsky.</summary></entry><entry><title>NYT reports plans for fresh strikes on Iran after the US midterm elections</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a70494a8214c519cbb7344455e367037cdad04658b1dad9f2a4b8e9a1b9559c0</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:21Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T08:40:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/nyt-reports-plans-for-fresh-strikes-on-iran-after-the-us-midterm-elections--22bada901bcb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/nyt-reports-plans-for-fresh-strikes-on-iran-after-the-us-midterm-elections" /><summary type="html">Reza Sayah, our correspondent in Tehran Iran, has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Netanyahu vows to ‘destroy’ Hebron after 2 soldiers killed in ‘terrorist attack’</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:43a755585427c9913bbe92220fb1adbc6796aea4211f72214c05eb59adcf3b9c</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:21Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T08:35:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261023-netanyahu-orders-army-to-prepare-for-full-west-bank-closure-after-attack--3d1dfabc7ef3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261023-netanyahu-orders-army-to-prepare-for-full-west-bank-closure-after-attack" /><summary type="html">Israel’s Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu on Friday vowed to “destroy” the Palestinian city of Hebron in the occupied West Bank after two Israeli soldiers were killed at a military checkpoint there. The two gunmen were also killed in the “terrorist attack”, the army said.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Israel's Ben-Gvir shares AI videos mocking Gazans as 'donkeys' and sending them to Paris</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:96912c525b141f2182f563ea3e6ae6c0bf5b5def13076021bbe7ac07c0a2fac5</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:21Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T19:38:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20261022-israel-s-ben-gvir-shares-ai-videos-mocking-gazans-as-donkeys-and-sending-them-to-paris--d0cf0d94b0cb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20261022-israel-s-ben-gvir-shares-ai-videos-mocking-gazans-as-donkeys-and-sending-them-to-paris" /><summary type="html">Israel's far-right minister Itamar Ben-Gvir is using AI-generated videos to mock Palestinians and push political messages ahead of the Israeli general election, including videos magically transporting Gazans to Paris or calling them "donkeys" for choosing to stay. One video has sparked an online spat with France. Artificial intelligence is playing a growing role in the campaign, with parties using deepfakes, bots and AI-generated content, raising concerns about disinformation and the technology's influence on voters.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>Ahead of US and Israeli elections, 3-day joint attack on Iran 'would not radically change conflict'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b62afa63571f2575b24c28f4c5a3a6108c3aaf760a04eba6911fc608ae15727d</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:21Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T16:36:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/ahead-of-us-and-israeli-elections-3-day-joint-attack-on-iran-would-not-radically-change-conflict--cb0fe2d52092.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ahead-of-us-and-israeli-elections-3-day-joint-attack-on-iran-would-not-radically-change-conflict" /><summary type="html">Jean-Emile Jammine is pleased to welcome Federico Donelli, Associate Professor of International Relations in the Department of Political and Social Sciences at the University of Trieste in Italy. Can another three days of military strikes achieve what eight months of confrontation have failed to deliver? Donelli challenges the assumption that a short, intensive offensive would necessarily produce a decisive political outcome. He argues, "the real question is whether military pressure is intended to constrain Iran's capacity, or to pressure Iran to sit on the table." And whether they can translate that capacity into a sustainable political outcome without provoking a wider regional crisis. Regardless, Donelli reminds us that "Iran still has leverage over the US."</summary></entry><entry><title>Reports show US and Israel are planning new strikes on Iran</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e68dbef897b7e28e3d576df87251421f9e121f4d71350fc7caf1397ac6162961</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:21Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T15:34:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261022-reports-show-us-and-israel-plan-new-strikes-on-iran--5077a10bc88b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261022-reports-show-us-and-israel-plan-new-strikes-on-iran" /><summary type="html">Reports claim that the US and Israel have ramped up military drills and planned new strikes in Iran, potentially targeting energy sites, drone facilities and missile arsenals. Details by FRANCE 24's correspondent in Jerusalem, Noga Tarnopolsky.</summary></entry></feed>
